  "practicalExamplesLabel": "Practical examples",
  "onboardingStep1Question": "Do you use customers in your business?",
  "onboardingStep1Paragraph1": "When enabled, you get the full customer module: a card for each customer, purchase history, and quick tracking from the invoice.",
  "onboardingStep1Paragraph2": "You can link every sale to a specific customer, which makes reporting easier later and creates a more consistent experience for repeat customers.",
  "onboardingStep1Paragraph3": "If you do a quick cash sale without a name, that stays available — enabling this doesn't force you to pick a customer every time.",
  "onboardingStep1Example1": "Example: a regular customer who buys daily — you save their name and quickly see their latest invoices.",
  "onboardingStep1Example2": "Example: when there's a debt or loyalty points, they show up linked to the same customer instead of manual searching.",
  "onboardingStep1SwitchLabel": "Enable customer module",
  "onboardingStep2Question": "Do you want a loyalty points program?",
  "onboardingStep2Paragraph1": "Loyalty gives customers points on purchases, which they can redeem according to rules you set in Settings.",
  "onboardingStep2Paragraph2": "The program is linked to customer profiles — the clearer your customer data, the easier it is to track.",
  "onboardingStep2Paragraph3": "You can turn the feature on now and adjust the earn/redeem rates later without redoing this wizard.",
  "onboardingStep2Example1": "Example: every 10,000 IQD earns 10 points, based on the rule you choose.",
  "onboardingStep2Example2": "Example: a customer who's collected enough points redeems them for a discount on a later invoice.",
  "onboardingStep2SwitchLabel": "Enable loyalty points",
  "onboardingStep2Footnote": "Requires the customer module enabled in the previous step; if it isn't, loyalty won't work until you re-enable customers.",
  "onboardingStep3Question": "Do you charge tax on sales?",
  "onboardingStep3Paragraph1": "When enabled, a clear tax field appears on the sales invoice so it's calculated consistently with the total.",
  "onboardingStep3Paragraph2": "Suitable for stores that apply a known tax rate on goods or services.",
  "onboardingStep3Paragraph3": "You can fine-tune the detailed behavior from POS settings after finishing this quick setup.",
  "onboardingStep3Example1": "Example: an invoice worth 100,000 IQD with a set tax percentage added on top.",
  "onboardingStep3Example2": "Example: the staff member sees the tax and final total within the same sales invoice.",
  "onboardingStep3SwitchLabel": "Show tax on sales invoice",
  "onboardingStep4Question": "Do you allow a discount on the invoice total?",
  "onboardingStep4Paragraph1": "An overall discount is useful for seasonal offers or negotiating price in front of the customer without changing each item's price.",
  "onboardingStep4Paragraph2": "The field appears on the sales screen so it completes the invoice without adding extra complexity for staff.",
  "onboardingStep4Paragraph3": "You can turn it off later if you decide to work with fixed prices only.",
  "onboardingStep4Example1": "Example: you give a flat 5,000 IQD discount on a large invoice.",
  "onboardingStep4Example2": "Example: a one-day special offer without changing the base product prices.",
  "onboardingStep4SwitchLabel": "Show overall discount on invoice",
  "onboardingStep5Question": "Do you sell on credit (deferred payment)?",
  "onboardingStep5Paragraph1": "Enabling this opens the debts panel and tracks amounts owed by each customer, with adjustable alerts and limits.",
  "onboardingStep5Paragraph2": "Suits merchants who trust known customers and need a clear record of deferred sales.",
  "onboardingStep5Paragraph3": "It doesn't stop cash sales — it just adds the option to record a sale as debt when selecting a customer with the right permissions.",
  "onboardingStep5Example1": "Example: a customer takes goods today and pays at the end of the week.",
  "onboardingStep5Example2": "Example: you check a customer's statement and clearly see what's paid and what's still owed.",
  "onboardingStep5SwitchLabel": "Enable credit sales and debts",
  "onboardingStep6Question": "Do you sell on installments?",
  "onboardingStep6Paragraph1": "Installment plans let you split an invoice's price into scheduled payments while tracking what's left owed by the customer.",
  "onboardingStep6Paragraph2": "Useful for higher-priced goods or long-term contracts.",
  "onboardingStep6Paragraph3": "The fine details of scheduling are managed from dedicated modules after finishing this setup.",
  "onboardingStep6Example1": "Example: a device worth 600,000 IQD paid over 6 monthly installments.",
  "onboardingStep6Example2": "Example: you see upcoming and overdue payments for each customer in one place.",
  "onboardingStep6SwitchLabel": "Enable installment sales",
  "onboardingStep7Question": "Do you sell by weight (kilo, gram, etc.)?",
  "onboardingStep7Paragraph1": "Enabling this prepares the sales interface and barcodes to support weights and decimal quantities where needed.",
  "onboardingStep7Paragraph2": "Suitable for groceries, hardware, or any business that relies on a scale.",
  "onboardingStep7Paragraph3": "You can configure weight-based barcode formats from advanced settings after this wizard.",
  "onboardingStep7Example1": "Example: selling 1.250 kg of a product instead of a single piece.",
  "onboardingStep7Example2": "Example: scanning a scale barcode that automatically contains the product's weight and price.",
  "onboardingStep7SwitchLabel": "Enable sales by weight",
  "onboardingStep8Question": "Do you sell clothing (colors and sizes)?",
  "onboardingStep8Paragraph1": "Enabling this prepares product and sales screens to support item variants (different colors and sizes of the same model).",
  "onboardingStep8Paragraph2": "Makes it easier to track stock for each color or size separately and shows a quick interactive picker at the time of sale.",
  "onboardingStep8Example1": "Example: a shirt available in blue and black, in sizes S, M, and L.",
  "onboardingStep8Example2": "Example: selecting a clothing item opens a quick popup to pick the available size and color in stock.",
  "onboardingStep8SwitchLabel": "Enable clothing and sizes module",
  "onboardingStep9Question": "Do you offer specific services (repairs, workshop, etc.)?",
  "onboardingStep9Paragraph1": "Enabling this reveals the full services and maintenance module: work tickets, service requests, and a services and pricing catalog.",
  "onboardingStep9Paragraph2": "Useful for workshops, service centers, and any business that provides services to customers alongside selling goods.",
  "onboardingStep9Example1": "Example: opening a maintenance ticket for a computer or car and setting the job status.",
  "onboardingStep9Example2": "Example: adding an installation or quick maintenance service to a sales invoice.",
  "onboardingStep9SwitchLabel": "Enable services and maintenance tickets",
